<span id="A5.F16.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F16.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem:
A line has slope <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{5}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{5}.</annotation></semantics></math> Which of the following vectors are possible direction vectors for the line?
<br class="ltx_break">pair x = (3,0), y = (0,2);
<br class="ltx_break">(A): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}2\\
5\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}2\\
5\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, y
<br class="ltx_break">(B): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}5\\
2\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}5\\
2\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, x + y
<br class="ltx_break">(C): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}0\\
0\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}0\\
0\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, 2*x + y
<br class="ltx_break">(D): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}-2\\
-5\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}-2\\
-5\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, 3*x + y
<br class="ltx_break">(E): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}-5\\
-2\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}-5\\
-2\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, (0,0)
<br class="ltx_break">(F): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}2/5\\
1\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}2/5\\
1\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, x
<br class="ltx_break">(G): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}40\\
16\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">40</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}40\\
16\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, 2*x
<br class="ltx_break">(H): <math id="A5.F16.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}4\\
10\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}4\\
10\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, 3*x</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.F16.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_figure_panel" height="156.09" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 156.09" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,156.09) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#818181;" fill="#818181" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 150.19 C 0 153.45 2.64 156.09 5.91 156.09 L 544.09 156.09 C 547.36 156.09 550 153.45 550 150.19 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 131.98 L 548.03 131.98 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 140.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F16.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.F16.pic2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F16.pic2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Answer: Max length 1024 + EOS confidence lowering</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:7.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="106.39" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 102.93)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F16.pic2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A5.F16.pic2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F16.pic2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The slope of the line is <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the direction vector of the line is <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}5\\
2\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}5\\
2\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the correct options are <span id="A5.F16.pic2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">B</span>, <span id="A5.F16.pic2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">G</span>, and <span id="A5.F16.pic2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">H</span>.
Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{B},\text{G},\text{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{B},\text{G},\text{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
Problem:
Let <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be a function such that <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\frac{1}{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\frac{1}{x}.</annotation></semantics></math> Find <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(2)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(2).</annotation></semantics></math>
Solution: Since <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\frac{1}{x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\frac{1}{x},</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(2)=\frac{1}{2}=\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></menclose></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(2)=\frac{1}{2}=\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
Problem:
Let <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\frac{1}{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\frac{1}{x}.</annotation></semantics></math> Find <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(2)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(2).</annotation></semantics></math>
Solution: Since <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\frac{1}{x}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\frac{1}{x},</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(2)=\frac{1}{2}=\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></menclose></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(2)=\frac{1}{2}=\boxed{\frac{1}{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="A5.F16.pic2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
…</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 16: </span>LLaDA-Instruct, MATH with 3-shots example. Decoding <span id="A5.F16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;eos&gt;</span> lastly by lowering the confidence artificially as in LLaDA 1.5, the model does not finish the answer appropriately, filling all available spaces with unrelated content tokens.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F17" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
